1
00:01:32,850 --> 00:01:35,020
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:37,610
[Episode 26]

3
00:01:39,479 --> 00:01:41,140
It has nothing to do with that.

4
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:42,920
Don't be mad.

5
00:01:43,479 --> 00:01:44,640
I'm not mad.

6
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,320
I think you're right.

7
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:48,310
I do have that problem.

8
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:49,420
I'll work on it.

9
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:52,200
It's fine.

10
00:01:52,410 --> 00:01:53,550
Let's go find Qiao Xiaojun again.

11
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:55,420
He definitely hasn't told us everything.

12
00:01:55,420 --> 00:01:56,280
Actually,
even if you hadn't said anything,

13
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:58,160
I was already starting to regret it.

14
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:59,000
I got a little too

15
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,040
pushy just now.

16
00:02:00,710 --> 00:02:01,920
The reality he has to face

17
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,580
is something we don't have to.

18
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:04,440
Of course,

19
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:05,230
that's not an excuse

20
00:02:05,230 --> 00:02:06,470
for him to defend himself like that.

21
00:02:06,470 --> 00:02:06,970
But we

22
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,240
can't expect others

23
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:10,199
to risk their own safety

24
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:11,360
and their livelihood

25
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:12,430
or even their well-being

26
00:02:12,430 --> 00:02:14,090
to challenge certain things.

27
00:02:21,470 --> 00:02:22,000
Tired?

28
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:25,090
Not really.

29
00:02:25,470 --> 00:02:26,470
It's just...

30
00:02:26,910 --> 00:02:27,970
I feel so helpless.

31
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:30,520
I don't know where to put my efforts.

32
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:36,530
You've already done incredibly well.

33
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:39,470
Really?

34
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:58,260
♪ The first light of dawn
spills across the table ♪

35
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:04,410
♪ Every stroke defines the line
between good and evil ♪

36
00:03:06,750 --> 00:03:09,160
♪ Behind every verdict ♪

37
00:03:09,190 --> 00:03:13,010
♪ Lie words left unspoken ♪

38
00:03:13,250 --> 00:03:21,260
♪ And souls left broken ♪

39
00:03:21,770 --> 00:03:22,900
♪ No need to ask him ♪

40
00:03:22,930 --> 00:03:27,710
♪ How reason and passion make peace ♪

41
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,360
Here, have some chicken.

42
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:27,520
It's nutritious.

43
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:29,000
Is it good?

44
00:03:29,450 --> 00:03:30,490
♪ Just watch him ♪

45
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:31,560
Drink it all.

46
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:35,890
♪ A light in hand,
keeping vigil at the edge of the abyss ♪

47
00:03:32,630 --> 00:03:34,490
I worked hard to make this for you.

48
00:03:36,990 --> 00:03:38,640
♪ On the scales ♪

49
00:03:38,670 --> 00:03:44,060
♪ Suffering weighs against our vows ♪

50
00:03:41,910 --> 00:03:42,640
Captain Lyu.

51
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,430
What do you think about that pager?

52
00:03:44,079 --> 00:03:45,510
♪ Who doesn't ♪

53
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:46,750
Back then you didn't tell us

54
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:51,650
♪ Weigh principle against compromise
within their conscience? ♪

55
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,870
to gather evidence proving his innocence.

56
00:03:48,870 --> 00:03:50,190
You've kept this all this time?

57
00:03:50,190 --> 00:03:51,120
Of course I have.

58
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,870
I'll keep it
until your consciences kick in,

59
00:03:53,870 --> 00:03:55,400
and until you figure it out.

60
00:03:57,570 --> 00:03:58,250
This case

61
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,590
was sent back by the procuratorate
and the court

62
00:03:59,590 --> 00:04:01,150
several times for further investigation.

63
00:04:01,150 --> 00:04:02,750
They all said we got it wrong.

64
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:04,590
You have no idea the pressure

65
00:04:04,590 --> 00:04:06,430
we were under to get him to trial.

66
00:04:07,490 --> 00:04:14,130
♪ Testimonies drift down like snowflakes ♪

67
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:08,110
Mentor.

68
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,530
I want to go to Nanlu.

69
00:04:10,180 --> 00:04:10,960
I don't have a pager.

70
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:11,860
You can't reach me,

71
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:13,270
unless I call you first.

72
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:15,870
Regarding this matter,

73
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:20,360
♪ Melting on a trembling fingertip ♪

74
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,529
whether to proceed or stop,

75
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:19,589
we'll talk about it when I get back.

76
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:23,070
Mentor,

77
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:25,400
♪ This garment of justice ♪

78
00:04:23,430 --> 00:04:24,680
for Hu Xudong's case,

79
00:04:24,830 --> 00:04:26,240
I want to be his defense lawyer.

80
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:29,100
♪ Sewn with threads of regret ♪

81
00:04:29,430 --> 00:04:30,190
Meeting with clients is tough.

82
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:36,690
♪ Through the ages,
it still rests on the shoulder ♪

83
00:04:30,630 --> 00:04:31,680
Reviewing case files is tough.

84
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:33,340
Gathering evidence is tough.

85
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:34,720
But the first two hurdles

86
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,850
shouldn't be a problem for you, right?

87
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:38,650
♪ Don’t ask ♪

88
00:04:38,670 --> 00:04:43,950
♪ How tears and the gavel meet ♪

89
00:04:45,330 --> 00:04:46,360
♪ Just watch him ♪

90
00:04:46,390 --> 00:04:51,810
♪ Rebuilding reality from nothingness ♪

91
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:54,380
♪ Inside and outside the statutes ♪

92
00:04:54,409 --> 00:04:59,770
♪ Standing yesterday and tomorrow ♪

93
00:04:59,790 --> 00:05:01,330
♪ Who doesn't ♪

94
00:05:01,350 --> 00:05:07,150
♪ Guard their dignity in shackles ♪

95
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:09,980
Come on, smile.

96
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:11,240
Okay.

97
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:14,000
Okay.

98
00:05:18,510 --> 00:05:19,510
Okay, you two, one more.

99
00:05:19,510 --> 00:05:20,240
Get closer.

100
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:21,190
Yes.

101
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:22,630
Get closer.

102
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:43,920
Aren't you putting these together?

103
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,130
I want to take it back to show my mentor.

104
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:47,460
Right.

105
00:05:48,390 --> 00:05:49,000
We should invite him

106
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,460
to be our wedding witness.

107
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:55,250
Zheng Jianmin.

108
00:05:58,270 --> 00:05:59,070
Do you love me?

109
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:04,570
I've never heard you say it.

110
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,500
That's pretty direct.

111
00:06:08,980 --> 00:06:09,910
I want to hear it.

112
00:06:12,630 --> 00:06:13,070
I do.

113
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:17,850
Say the whole thing.

114
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:22,650
Zhang Lihui,

115
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:24,750
I love you.

116
00:06:28,270 --> 00:06:29,270
Very, very much.

117
00:06:30,530 --> 00:06:31,360
You are the most important person

118
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,270
in my life.

119
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:35,040
I...

120
00:06:35,950 --> 00:06:37,360
I thought that in my life,

121
00:06:38,370 --> 00:06:39,200
no one would ever

122
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:40,400
say these words to me.

123
00:06:46,630 --> 00:06:47,560
I'm quite happy.

124
00:07:02,950 --> 00:07:04,360
We got our marriage license this morning,

125
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:06,220
and we're apart by the afternoon.

126
00:07:07,310 --> 00:07:08,440
Afraid I'll run off?

127
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:10,160
Nope.

128
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:12,850
I'm protected by the marriage law now.

129
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:15,970
I have to go back.

130
00:07:16,650 --> 00:07:17,720
Otherwise, my mentor won't be able

131
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,250
to answer to his superiors.

132
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:20,920
Still no progress

133
00:07:21,430 --> 00:07:22,630
this time around.

134
00:07:23,370 --> 00:07:24,310
I'm afraid we're in

135
00:07:24,310 --> 00:07:25,310
for the long haul.

136
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,520
Then you'll be stuck in Bieshan?

137
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:28,850
To be honest,

138
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:31,220
my mentor has been urging me to leave.

139
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:32,270
In the past,

140
00:07:32,909 --> 00:07:34,480
I felt whether I was transferred back

141
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:35,680
or stayed in Bieshan,

142
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,090
I was alone anyway,

143
00:07:37,090 --> 00:07:38,220
so it didn't matter.

144
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:40,390
But now I have you.

145
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,650
It's different.

146
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,240
And I just feel

147
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,130
so bad for my mentor.

148
00:07:49,870 --> 00:07:50,310
Yeah.

149
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:53,040
We have to be loyal and grateful.

150
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:55,840
You can't just forget him
now that you've got a man.

151
00:07:55,870 --> 00:07:57,670
Thank you for understanding me.

152
00:07:59,950 --> 00:08:00,560
So do you

153
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:01,870
actually want me

154
00:08:01,870 --> 00:08:03,200
to transfer back or not?

155
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,750
I'd be lying if I said no.

156
00:08:06,190 --> 00:08:07,600
Your husband's not that tough.

157
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:08,730
Of course I miss you.

158
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,370
We'll figure it out.

159
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,820
We've got our whole lives.

160
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:23,800
What's wrong?

161
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:30,480
Hey. There are people around.

162
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:32,470
It's legal. I don't care.

163
00:08:33,620 --> 00:08:35,549
Still, it's embarrassing.

164
00:08:39,549 --> 00:08:40,610
Is that the reason?

165
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,289
For Xia Yingjie?

166
00:08:45,030 --> 00:08:46,360
She is a big part of it.

167
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:50,150
But I also couldn't stand to see

168
00:08:50,150 --> 00:08:51,610
Hu Xudong's case turn into

169
00:08:52,390 --> 00:08:53,720
a wrongful conviction.

170
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,680
I know I'm useless, Mr. Zhou.

171
00:08:58,360 --> 00:08:59,420
Go ahead, scold me.

172
00:08:59,670 --> 00:09:00,030
I...

173
00:09:04,910 --> 00:09:06,270
What are you laughing at?

174
00:09:06,270 --> 00:09:07,440
Say something too.

175
00:09:07,990 --> 00:09:09,320
I'm happy for him.

176
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:13,040
Amending law is important, sure.

177
00:09:13,170 --> 00:09:14,050
But for the ones

178
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:15,000
you love,

179
00:09:15,020 --> 00:09:16,950
burning yourself out, no regrets—

180
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:19,920
everyone should have that
once in their life.

181
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,080
Otherwise, you'll regret it
when you're old.

182
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:22,820
Soup's here.

183
00:09:23,910 --> 00:09:24,970
I support Yizhong.

184
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,440
Yizhong is right.

185
00:09:28,030 --> 00:09:29,630
That's what I call a real man.

186
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:32,360
There's plenty of people
working on the amendment.

187
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:33,960
There will be other chances.

188
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,900
But you only get one true love.

189
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,600
Miss that, and it's gone.

190
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:39,630
We only live once,

191
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:40,600
right?

192
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:44,480
You should stick with criminal defense.

193
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:45,880
Still on the front lines.

194
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,630
You're not like this guy,

195
00:09:47,870 --> 00:09:49,600
always chasing after money.

196
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:51,270
Why am I always

197
00:09:51,270 --> 00:09:52,440
the bad example?

198
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:53,730
What did I do?

199
00:09:54,150 --> 00:09:54,830
Lu Zeming.

200
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:56,120
Don't deny it.

201
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,510
Look at all the famous lawyers out there.

202
00:09:58,510 --> 00:10:00,000
They all do criminal defense.

203
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:00,840
See?

204
00:10:01,090 --> 00:10:02,000
Old Zhou, if you want to talk,

205
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,790
go talk to your brilliant student here.

206
00:10:03,790 --> 00:10:05,080
He's at our firm now.

207
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,360
And he's handling criminal cases too.

208
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:09,290
I don't have such grand ambitions.

209
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:11,930
Right, Yizhong.

210
00:10:12,250 --> 00:10:13,000
Do you really think

211
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,260
there's a problem with Hu Xudong's case?

212
00:10:17,630 --> 00:10:18,600
I'm not saying

213
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:20,320
there's definitely anything wrong

214
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,370
with this case.

215
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:23,320
Actually, I'm treating it

216
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:24,340
as a practical exercise

217
00:10:24,340 --> 00:10:25,740
for the legal amendment.

218
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:27,150
I'll keep you both posted

219
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:28,120
on any issues

220
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,030
that come up.

221
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,980
I keep telling myself,

222
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:32,130
and Yingjie too,

223
00:10:32,470 --> 00:10:33,870
that we absolutely cannot let our biases

224
00:10:33,870 --> 00:10:34,930
lead us by the nose.

225
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:38,770
Investigation-centered,

226
00:10:39,550 --> 00:10:41,280
judicial bureaucratization,

227
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,120
confession before evidence,

228
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:44,380
presumption of guilt,

229
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:47,360
extended detention,
and coerced confessions—

230
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,840
you're likely to encounter

231
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:50,390
all of these down the road.

232
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:54,120
These are

233
00:10:54,260 --> 00:10:55,200
precisely the issues we aim to address

234
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:57,260
in the major revision of the two laws.

235
00:10:57,390 --> 00:10:58,200
However,

236
00:10:58,790 --> 00:10:59,630
the road ahead

237
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,130
is long and arduous.

238
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:07,320
Alright.

239
00:11:08,030 --> 00:11:09,910
I support you going back down there.

240
00:11:09,910 --> 00:11:11,550
When you come back,

241
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:14,160
your perspective will have broadened.

242
00:11:16,070 --> 00:11:18,120
With both of you supporting me,

243
00:11:18,630 --> 00:11:20,200
that's half the pressure off.

244
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:21,660
What about the other half?

245
00:11:22,030 --> 00:11:22,670
Yizhong,

246
00:11:22,920 --> 00:11:24,320
don't listen to your dad.

247
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,480
He can't control you.

248
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,480
Just like you,

249
00:11:27,190 --> 00:11:27,910
always stirring up trouble?

250
00:11:27,910 --> 00:11:28,320
I…

251
00:11:28,870 --> 00:11:29,480
Yizhong,

252
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:31,480
if needed,

253
00:11:34,390 --> 00:11:35,590
I can talk to your dad.

254
00:11:36,910 --> 00:11:37,790
Your dad

255
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,900
takes things too heavily.

256
00:11:41,510 --> 00:11:42,200
Actually,

257
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,980
you should try to understand him.

258
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:47,620
After all, our generation...

259
00:11:52,990 --> 00:11:54,250
If the chance comes up,

260
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:55,860
communicate with him.

261
00:11:58,440 --> 00:12:00,100
Times are pushing us forward.

262
00:12:01,390 --> 00:12:03,590
We can't always be burdened by the past.

263
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:08,790
Here.

264
00:12:09,330 --> 00:12:10,000
Come on, let's have a drink.

265
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:10,960
Getting a bit heavy, huh?

266
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:12,200
Alright, let's raise our glasses.

267
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:12,660
Cheers.

268
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,530
A toast to send Yizhong off.

269
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:19,720
Here.

270
00:12:29,910 --> 00:12:30,600
This case

271
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:32,550
will eventually go to Yu Gaoyuan

272
00:12:32,550 --> 00:12:33,680
and his team, right?

273
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,120
Well, well, old rivals, huh?

274
00:12:41,030 --> 00:12:42,390
He's the Deputy Court Pres.

275
00:12:42,390 --> 00:12:43,950
If any problems come up,

276
00:12:44,410 --> 00:12:45,510
he can pull some weight

277
00:12:45,510 --> 00:12:46,750
with the Adjudication Committee.

278
00:12:46,750 --> 00:12:47,390
The question is,

279
00:12:47,390 --> 00:12:49,190
what kind of weight will he pull?

280
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,290
Hopefully for the good.

281
00:12:51,290 --> 00:12:53,020
Not working against us, right?

282
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:56,280
I'm not trying to stir things up.

283
00:12:56,390 --> 00:12:57,550
Yu Gaoyuan

284
00:12:57,750 --> 00:12:58,880
is not bad by nature.

285
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:01,320
His professional skills are quite high.

286
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,550
It's just... how should I put it?

287
00:13:02,550 --> 00:13:03,100
He's a bit

288
00:13:03,670 --> 00:13:04,270
slippery.

289
00:13:04,630 --> 00:13:05,240
You know?

290
00:13:05,370 --> 00:13:07,570
Hard to know what he's really thinking.

291
00:13:08,550 --> 00:13:10,550
I believe he still has convictions.

292
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:14,980
Call you dumb,

293
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:16,720
but you've got a higher degree than me.

294
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:17,910
Call you smart,

295
00:13:18,670 --> 00:13:20,870
but sometimes you're pretty clueless.

296
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:24,480
You'd better be careful.

297
00:13:25,270 --> 00:13:25,870
I know.

298
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:27,390
After all these years,

299
00:13:27,390 --> 00:13:29,250
haven't we always been like this?

300
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:30,270
Later,

301
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:32,680
I might still need your help.

302
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:34,060
Give me a break.

303
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:36,270
I took a leave
and have to go back to Nanyu.

304
00:13:36,270 --> 00:13:37,340
My wife's pregnancy

305
00:13:37,340 --> 00:13:37,960
is pretty rough.

306
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,030
I need to be there with her.

307
00:13:39,030 --> 00:13:39,690
Otherwise,

308
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:41,840
old Ding would've

309
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:43,840
served me a summons already.

310
00:13:51,270 --> 00:13:52,870
The chief doesn't have many things.

311
00:13:52,870 --> 00:13:54,400
He lived a very simple life.

312
00:13:55,510 --> 00:13:57,170
Do you need me to help you pack?

313
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:58,120
No, I've got it.

314
00:13:58,360 --> 00:13:58,960
Thank you.

315
00:13:59,000 --> 00:13:59,330
Okay.

316
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,960
Call me if you need anything.

317
00:14:36,150 --> 00:14:39,120
[Notice of Deep Condolences
for Fang Leiming]

318
00:14:50,630 --> 00:14:51,560
My condolences.

319
00:15:11,210 --> 00:15:11,780
Haohao.

320
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:13,720
Uncle.

321
00:15:16,630 --> 00:15:17,890
This is Grandpa Huang.

322
00:15:25,670 --> 00:15:26,530
Get out of here!

323
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:28,870
You ungrateful wretch.

324
00:15:30,030 --> 00:15:30,630
All these years,

325
00:15:30,630 --> 00:15:33,560
how many times have you visited
your father-in-law?

326
00:15:34,270 --> 00:15:35,030
When he was in the hospital,

327
00:15:35,030 --> 00:15:36,830
how many times did you visit him?

328
00:15:40,550 --> 00:15:41,240
Haohao,

329
00:15:41,270 --> 00:15:42,020
how could you marry

330
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:43,500
such a jerk?

331
00:16:00,630 --> 00:16:02,000
Go back. He's gone.

332
00:16:02,690 --> 00:16:04,020
He had a few drinks

333
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,100
when he came today.

334
00:16:05,390 --> 00:16:06,530
Plus, he's grieving.

335
00:16:06,530 --> 00:16:07,660
He was a bit out of it.

336
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:08,360
He's my dad's

337
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:10,090
comrade-in-arms for decades.

338
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:11,270
Don't take it to heart.

339
00:16:11,270 --> 00:16:11,910
I didn't.

340
00:16:13,870 --> 00:16:16,400
Mr. Huang isn't the only one
who calls me that.

341
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:17,900
I brought home

342
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:19,960
the diary Dad wrote. Have you read it?

343
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,240
"Ungrateful wretch"
and "my good daughter."

344
00:16:21,240 --> 00:16:23,240
All about Fang Haohao this and that.

345
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:27,580
I'm not even in the family photo
on the table.

346
00:16:30,340 --> 00:16:31,100
Truth is, he never really treated me

347
00:16:31,100 --> 00:16:31,820
as family.

348
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:33,630
Sorry. I shouldn't have said...

349
00:16:33,630 --> 00:16:34,490
What about you?

350
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:38,610
Did you treat him as family?

351
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:48,960
Then I guess we're even.

352
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:50,750
My parents are also outsiders

353
00:16:50,750 --> 00:16:51,480
to you.

354
00:16:51,750 --> 00:16:52,550
That's you...

355
00:16:53,550 --> 00:16:54,150
Forget it.

356
00:17:02,670 --> 00:17:04,440
Since we've become so distant,

357
00:17:05,490 --> 00:17:06,310
is there even any point

358
00:17:06,310 --> 00:17:07,970
to keep this family together?

359
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:12,569
What do you mean?

360
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:15,250
Running away from home?

361
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:18,400
I quit my job.

362
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:21,490
And then?

363
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,260
I want to go to Beijing.

364
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:27,859
A classmate found me a job.

365
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:29,160
A joint venture.

366
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:31,270
The pay's a bit higher,

367
00:17:31,270 --> 00:17:32,590
but not that much.

368
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:37,720
I just need some breathing room.

369
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:39,520
Otherwise I'll lose my mind.

370
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:42,200
So I have to take Diandian by myself?

371
00:17:43,070 --> 00:17:44,600
I'll figure something out.

372
00:17:45,110 --> 00:17:46,510
If it really doesn't work,

373
00:17:46,510 --> 00:17:47,840
I'll take her to Beijing

374
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:50,160
and leave her with my aunt.

375
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:52,070
She works at the Ministry of Railways.

376
00:17:52,070 --> 00:17:53,130
She can arrange it.

377
00:17:55,590 --> 00:17:56,240
Okay. Go.

378
00:18:01,070 --> 00:18:01,730
Yu Gaoyuan.

379
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:03,270
I never thought...

380
00:18:03,270 --> 00:18:03,790
Stop.

381
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:05,350
You can go wherever you want.

382
00:18:05,350 --> 00:18:06,270
But we can't get a divorce.

383
00:18:06,270 --> 00:18:08,670
Diandian can't grow up without her mother.

384
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:32,000
This is the victim,

385
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,070
Yin Ping's uncle.

386
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:35,010
He works as a journalist

387
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:36,110
in Guangzhou.

388
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:38,790
Where did this uncle pop up from?

389
00:18:38,790 --> 00:18:40,240
He's not some stone‑born monkey.

390
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,640
Of course he has an uncle.

391
00:18:43,070 --> 00:18:45,400
He went back to his hometown
a few days ago.

392
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:46,880
He collected signatures

393
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:48,400
from over two hundred villagers

394
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:50,130
and drafted a petition letter.

395
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:52,440
He sent it to the Public Security Bureau
and the Procuratorate.

396
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:54,570
The court should have received it too.

397
00:18:57,360 --> 00:18:58,160
This case

398
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:01,100
is already public knowledge.

399
00:19:03,030 --> 00:19:04,790
Can't have officials colluding.

400
00:19:04,790 --> 00:19:07,390
We demand severe punishment
for the murderer.

401
00:19:07,810 --> 00:19:08,370
Hu Xudong

402
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,330
indeed has a relative

403
00:19:09,330 --> 00:19:10,970
who works as a township cadre.

404
00:19:10,970 --> 00:19:11,720
But I looked into it.

405
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:13,450
He's just a low-level staffer.

406
00:19:13,550 --> 00:19:15,240
And there's no evidence showing

407
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:16,400
that he covered anything up.

408
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:18,400
The public doesn't care about that.

409
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:19,980
Look what it says here:

410
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:22,650
''Resort to media if necessary.''

411
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:24,790
He is a journalist himself.

412
00:19:24,790 --> 00:19:25,790
That's his trade.

413
00:19:25,830 --> 00:19:27,510
You want to see public outrage?

414
00:19:27,510 --> 00:19:29,480
You want to see people
clamoring for blood?

415
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:30,480
This is it!

416
00:19:31,790 --> 00:19:32,990
Don't you think about

417
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:36,330
the pressure the Public Security Bureau
is under right now?

418
00:19:40,270 --> 00:19:40,720
Hello?

419
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:42,240
What?

420
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:44,350
Where?

421
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:47,480
Okay.

422
00:19:48,030 --> 00:19:48,640
Let me see.

423
00:20:06,450 --> 00:20:09,070
[Severely Punish Hu Xudong!
Justice for Our Dead!]

424
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:24,860
Come in.

425
00:20:25,030 --> 00:20:25,640
Ms. Gui,

426
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:27,300
please come in.

427
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:28,510
This way.

428
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,070
Look,

429
00:20:32,150 --> 00:20:33,460
our law firm,

430
00:20:34,180 --> 00:20:36,030
whether in terms of scale

431
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:37,180
or expertise,

432
00:20:37,620 --> 00:20:39,180
even in the provincial capital,

433
00:20:39,180 --> 00:20:40,720
is quite impressive.

434
00:20:41,590 --> 00:20:42,240
Come on in.

435
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:46,090
This is our law firm.

436
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:47,790
Please, this is our office.

437
00:20:47,790 --> 00:20:48,400
Zhao.

438
00:20:50,590 --> 00:20:51,450
Get some water.

439
00:20:52,750 --> 00:20:53,950
Let me introduce you.

440
00:20:54,830 --> 00:20:55,440
Ms. Gui,

441
00:20:56,530 --> 00:20:57,460
from Guangzhou,

442
00:20:57,590 --> 00:20:59,210
is a successful businesswoman.

443
00:20:59,210 --> 00:21:00,940
What's going on with you?

444
00:21:01,870 --> 00:21:03,040
Quick, make tea.

445
00:21:07,270 --> 00:21:08,230
Mr. Qin,

446
00:21:09,330 --> 00:21:10,610
seeing your office

447
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:11,570
so professional

448
00:21:11,790 --> 00:21:12,920
puts my mind at ease.

449
00:21:13,510 --> 00:21:14,440
I'm sorry.

450
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:16,900
Yesterday,
I thought you were a scammer too.

451
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:20,110
Nanyu

452
00:21:20,830 --> 00:21:21,720
is a bit poor,

453
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:23,520
but it's not like

454
00:21:23,550 --> 00:21:24,810
everyone is a scammer.

455
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:26,590
Don't say that.

456
00:21:27,070 --> 00:21:27,960
At first,

457
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:29,090
I really thought so.

458
00:21:30,920 --> 00:21:32,120
Most people are good,

459
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:33,000
truly.

460
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:35,090
Where is the tea?

461
00:21:36,590 --> 00:21:37,960
Five percent of two million.

462
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:38,690
Fair enough.

463
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:40,160
That's 100,000 yuan.

464
00:21:40,790 --> 00:21:42,430
As long as they deliver the goods

465
00:21:42,430 --> 00:21:43,790
or issue a refund per the contract,

466
00:21:43,790 --> 00:21:44,790
I'll pay you.

467
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:47,030
But

468
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:48,810
no upfront payment.

469
00:21:49,270 --> 00:21:50,790
I've been burned too many times.

470
00:21:50,790 --> 00:21:51,310
Sorry

471
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:52,380
if I'm being blunt.

472
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,080
Excuse me.

473
00:21:54,220 --> 00:21:55,050
You mean

474
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:56,520
five percent?

475
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,640
Seven percent. Deal?

476
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:02,820
How about this?

477
00:22:03,290 --> 00:22:05,220
I'll pay you even if we only recover

478
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:06,210
half the funds.

479
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:11,160
Ms. Gui.

480
00:22:11,750 --> 00:22:12,200
Well,

481
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:15,550
I have to discuss it

482
00:22:16,030 --> 00:22:16,960
with my partner.

483
00:22:19,720 --> 00:22:20,380
Have a seat.

484
00:22:30,480 --> 00:22:32,880
100,000 yuan. 100,000 yuan. 100,000 yuan.

485
00:22:35,070 --> 00:22:35,880
Stay calm.

486
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:45,550
Five, four, three, two,

487
00:22:45,550 --> 00:22:46,920
-Qin, Qin.
-one.

488
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:49,030
That woman, your big client?

489
00:22:49,030 --> 00:22:49,560
Get lost!

490
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:06,400
Ms. Gui,

491
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:08,880
my partner said

492
00:23:10,510 --> 00:23:11,590
fifteen percent.

493
00:23:13,110 --> 00:23:14,740
Debt‑recovery work like this

494
00:23:14,740 --> 00:23:15,720
usually calls for

495
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:17,550
a thirty‑percent cut.

496
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:21,740
Fifteen percent is way too high.

497
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:23,720
In Nanyu, you won't find

498
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:24,910
a better lawyer.

499
00:23:25,160 --> 00:23:26,160
It's us or nobody.

500
00:23:27,360 --> 00:23:28,890
Forgive me for being blunt.

501
00:23:32,830 --> 00:23:34,110
Let me make a phone call first.

502
00:23:34,110 --> 00:23:34,480
Okay.

503
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:45,860
What happened?

504
00:23:46,350 --> 00:23:47,950
Did your wife beat you again?

505
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:52,780
Let me tell you,

506
00:23:52,890 --> 00:23:53,680
that divorce case of yours,

507
00:23:53,680 --> 00:23:54,680
the 450 yuan,

508
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:56,430
not a penny is collected so far.

509
00:23:56,640 --> 00:23:57,880
You are planning to do this one
for free too.

510
00:23:57,880 --> 00:23:58,440
Right?

511
00:23:58,560 --> 00:23:59,370
I...

512
00:24:00,030 --> 00:24:01,000
A big client.

513
00:24:06,550 --> 00:24:07,680
Fine, fifteen it is.

514
00:24:07,830 --> 00:24:08,760
No other choice.

515
00:24:09,070 --> 00:24:10,530
It's our last‑ditch shot.

516
00:24:16,110 --> 00:24:16,590
Ms. Gui.

517
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:17,860
How about this?

518
00:24:18,550 --> 00:24:19,720
Let's call it friends.

519
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:20,680
Ten percent.

520
00:24:20,920 --> 00:24:21,440
Deal?

521
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:24,480
Deal.

522
00:24:28,290 --> 00:24:32,170
[Municipal Court Annual Summary
and Awards Ceremony]

523
00:24:28,670 --> 00:24:29,390
Finally,

524
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:32,150
in recognition of Comrade Guo Dajie's

525
00:24:32,510 --> 00:24:35,170
dedication,
overcoming countless hardships,

526
00:24:35,270 --> 00:24:37,750
and 28 years of loyal service,

527
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:39,440
this court has applied for

528
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:40,960
and received approval
from higher authorities,

529
00:24:40,960 --> 00:24:42,270
to award Comrade Guo Dajie

530
00:24:42,270 --> 00:24:44,800
an Individual Second-Class Merit citation.

531
00:25:05,590 --> 00:25:08,290
[Linshan City People's Procuratorate]

532
00:25:07,790 --> 00:25:08,530
Let me see.

533
00:25:10,790 --> 00:25:11,270
Guo,

534
00:25:11,720 --> 00:25:13,550
aren't you going home
for dumplings tonight?

535
00:25:13,550 --> 00:25:14,680
Dumplings?

536
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:15,820
Got to get back.

537
00:25:16,310 --> 00:25:17,370
Tell your wife

538
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:19,010
I'm not some slave‑driver.

539
00:25:19,110 --> 00:25:20,840
You're the one who never stops.

540
00:25:21,770 --> 00:25:25,170
A Communist Party member's job
is to fight the slave drivers.

541
00:25:27,360 --> 00:25:27,840
Lihui.

542
00:25:28,590 --> 00:25:30,000
You want to follow in
your mentor's footsteps?

543
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:32,110
This Second‑Class Merit doesn't come easy.

544
00:25:32,110 --> 00:25:32,640
You'd still have to

545
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:34,030
grind it out here for years.

546
00:25:34,030 --> 00:25:34,510
Yes.

547
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:37,000
Lihui is leaving.

548
00:25:40,950 --> 00:25:41,820
Where to?

549
00:25:42,720 --> 00:25:43,480
Nanlu.

550
00:25:44,240 --> 00:25:44,830
Mentor.

551
00:25:45,200 --> 00:25:46,200
Hold your tongue.

552
00:25:48,030 --> 00:25:49,890
Can our procuratorate let her go?

553
00:25:50,110 --> 00:25:50,840
A transfer

554
00:25:51,270 --> 00:25:53,600
to the municipal procuratorate in Nanlu.

555
00:25:56,310 --> 00:25:57,710
Such a great talent.

556
00:25:58,310 --> 00:26:00,660
The procuratorate will have to
give it serious consideration.

557
00:26:00,660 --> 00:26:02,060
Lihui, have you decided?

558
00:26:02,680 --> 00:26:04,030
Prosecutor You, actually I...

559
00:26:04,030 --> 00:26:05,510
Let me talk about something else.

560
00:26:05,510 --> 00:26:06,160
Lihui,

561
00:26:06,680 --> 00:26:07,680
go wait for me in the car

562
00:26:07,680 --> 00:26:08,720
for a moment.

563
00:26:09,070 --> 00:26:10,200
Go on, be a good girl.

564
00:26:10,240 --> 00:26:11,330
Get in the car. Go on.

565
00:26:11,330 --> 00:26:12,400
Go on, shoo.

566
00:26:13,240 --> 00:26:14,560
What's going on?

567
00:26:14,590 --> 00:26:15,720
What do you mean?

568
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:17,990
She'll talk to you when the time comes.

569
00:26:18,310 --> 00:26:21,110
You'll definitely
support her unconditionally.

570
00:26:29,970 --> 00:26:30,640
Guo Dajie,

571
00:26:31,440 --> 00:26:33,840
you two have formed
your own little clique,

572
00:26:33,850 --> 00:26:35,590
sneaking around all day like you're on

573
00:26:35,590 --> 00:26:36,920
some covert operation.

574
00:26:37,110 --> 00:26:38,440
Are you trying to rebel?

575
00:26:38,710 --> 00:26:40,140
Watch your mouth.

576
00:26:41,200 --> 00:26:43,800
I'm a recipient
of the Second‑Class Merit now.

577
00:26:47,680 --> 00:26:48,610
Alright, enough joking.

578
00:26:48,610 --> 00:26:49,340
I'm serious.

579
00:26:51,270 --> 00:26:52,790
Tell me the truth.

580
00:26:53,110 --> 00:26:53,750
Can this

581
00:26:54,340 --> 00:26:55,540
be used as

582
00:26:55,560 --> 00:26:57,620
a get-out-of-jail-free card later?

583
00:26:57,640 --> 00:26:58,570
What do you mean?

584
00:26:58,960 --> 00:27:01,030
Are you planning to take it
with you on a robbery?

585
00:27:01,030 --> 00:27:02,440
No, nothing like that.

586
00:27:03,070 --> 00:27:03,920
I mean,

587
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:05,550
what if one day

588
00:27:06,560 --> 00:27:08,400
I step out of line

589
00:27:08,850 --> 00:27:10,610
and upset the leaders,

590
00:27:11,750 --> 00:27:13,350
causing you headaches.

591
00:27:13,470 --> 00:27:14,370
Could you maybe

592
00:27:14,400 --> 00:27:15,720
cut me some slack?

593
00:27:16,070 --> 00:27:17,720
Just for its sake.

594
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:21,080
Were you ever in line before?

595
00:27:21,130 --> 00:27:22,610
Just this past year,

596
00:27:22,640 --> 00:27:23,310
with that Yan Jicai case—

597
00:27:23,310 --> 00:27:25,440
haven't you caused me enough trouble?

598
00:27:26,590 --> 00:27:28,590
That's exactly what I mean.

599
00:27:28,830 --> 00:27:30,690
Wait, you still haven't given up?

600
00:27:31,750 --> 00:27:33,080
You're about to retire.

601
00:27:33,440 --> 00:27:34,570
Don't you know that?

602
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:37,000
This isn't something
that gets resolved overnight.

603
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:37,880
That's why

604
00:27:38,750 --> 00:27:40,000
Lihui can't

605
00:27:40,030 --> 00:27:41,560
waste her time on this case.

606
00:27:41,750 --> 00:27:42,680
She has to leave.

607
00:27:42,750 --> 00:27:43,610
What about you?

608
00:27:44,550 --> 00:27:46,150
What do I have to hold me back?

609
00:27:46,880 --> 00:27:48,200
I'll just keep grinding.

610
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:48,760
I'm

611
00:27:48,960 --> 00:27:50,270
still so young.

612
00:27:53,510 --> 00:27:54,200
Guo.

613
00:27:55,080 --> 00:27:56,560
What can I even say to you?

614
00:27:56,970 --> 00:27:59,450
Then don't say anything.

615
00:28:00,570 --> 00:28:01,170
You.

616
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:03,610
Keep this for me.

617
00:28:03,800 --> 00:28:04,440
No, no.

618
00:28:04,460 --> 00:28:05,290
You, you, you...

619
00:28:05,290 --> 00:28:06,820
Listen to me. Listen to me.

620
00:28:07,640 --> 00:28:08,640
When you hate me,

621
00:28:09,590 --> 00:28:10,990
take it out and look at it.

622
00:28:11,790 --> 00:28:13,250
Remember the good things.

623
00:28:14,750 --> 00:28:15,790
I do not

624
00:28:16,760 --> 00:28:18,040
deserve this medal

625
00:28:18,070 --> 00:28:19,330
if I fail to get closure

626
00:28:20,070 --> 00:28:21,790
on this case.

627
00:28:22,880 --> 00:28:24,140
I wouldn't feel right.

628
00:28:25,790 --> 00:28:26,590
I'm leaving.

629
00:29:05,030 --> 00:29:06,560
Still mad at me?

630
00:29:15,540 --> 00:29:16,340
Lihui.

631
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:25,640
It's my fault

632
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:28,740
for making this decision for you.

633
00:29:29,720 --> 00:29:32,200
I deserve it if you blame me.

634
00:29:33,550 --> 00:29:34,310
Lihui,

635
00:29:35,290 --> 00:29:37,050
my wife and I

636
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:40,400
have lived apart all our lives.

637
00:29:41,880 --> 00:29:44,400
I owe her so much.

638
00:29:45,440 --> 00:29:46,970
I can never make it up to her.

639
00:29:49,310 --> 00:29:50,800
I was too selfish.

640
00:29:53,810 --> 00:29:56,300
I know you care about me.

641
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:00,070
But what normal wife

642
00:30:00,830 --> 00:30:01,590
wouldn't want to

643
00:30:01,590 --> 00:30:03,880
be with her husband?

644
00:30:05,070 --> 00:30:07,070
You didn't have a family growing up.

645
00:30:07,640 --> 00:30:08,970
Now that you've finally

646
00:30:09,520 --> 00:30:10,720
built one of your own.

647
00:30:12,150 --> 00:30:14,240
You need to nurture

648
00:30:14,680 --> 00:30:16,480
and cherish it.

649
00:30:18,030 --> 00:30:20,240
But this so-called "family"—

650
00:30:22,140 --> 00:30:24,470
it's really just the daily grind,

651
00:30:24,680 --> 00:30:26,240
and living a real life.

652
00:30:26,920 --> 00:30:28,310
I figured

653
00:30:29,070 --> 00:30:29,850
you might

654
00:30:29,880 --> 00:30:31,740
hesitate to bring it up yourself,

655
00:30:32,070 --> 00:30:34,040
so I took the initiative.

656
00:30:34,240 --> 00:30:35,350
So I...

657
00:30:38,550 --> 00:30:39,110
Just...

658
00:30:40,110 --> 00:30:42,480
Just forgive me.

659
00:30:45,310 --> 00:30:46,510
Will you, Kiddo?

660
00:30:53,350 --> 00:30:55,960
Let's put this behind us, alright?

661
00:31:01,130 --> 00:31:04,400
[Court President's Office]

662
00:31:03,500 --> 00:31:05,530
That's the situation.

663
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:07,690
I've been there several times.

664
00:31:07,790 --> 00:31:09,920
But the civil division doesn't

665
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:11,100
seem too eager.

666
00:31:11,200 --> 00:31:12,590
They keep putting it off.

667
00:31:12,590 --> 00:31:14,720
That's why I came to you.

668
00:31:19,360 --> 00:31:20,360
Tell me the truth.

669
00:31:21,030 --> 00:31:23,440
How did you meet that businesswoman?

670
00:31:26,480 --> 00:31:28,480
She sought me out for my reputation.

671
00:31:28,510 --> 00:31:29,640
Does your wife know?

672
00:31:32,880 --> 00:31:34,890
If your wife finds out

673
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:37,240
there's some businesswoman out there

674
00:31:37,270 --> 00:31:38,990
who's so into you.

675
00:31:39,440 --> 00:31:40,200
Qin Zhigao.

676
00:31:44,110 --> 00:31:45,690
Thank you for your concern,
Court Pres. Ding.

677
00:31:45,690 --> 00:31:47,620
I promise she won't mess things up.

678
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:49,500
So what do you think

679
00:31:50,510 --> 00:31:51,440
about this case?

680
00:31:56,310 --> 00:31:57,710
Let me see the documents.

681
00:31:57,830 --> 00:31:59,800
We'll handle it according to the law.

682
00:31:59,800 --> 00:32:01,520
The county is currently

683
00:32:01,550 --> 00:32:02,880
attracting investment

684
00:32:02,960 --> 00:32:04,670
and expanding business opportunities.

685
00:32:04,670 --> 00:32:05,960
We can't let certain individuals

686
00:32:05,960 --> 00:32:07,960
ruin Nanyu's business reputation.

687
00:32:09,510 --> 00:32:10,270
If it really is

688
00:32:10,270 --> 00:32:11,400
as you say,

689
00:32:11,830 --> 00:32:14,000
then we will handle it impartially.

690
00:32:15,510 --> 00:32:17,200
Thank you, Court Pres. Ding.

691
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:19,070
You've really

692
00:32:19,400 --> 00:32:21,060
done me a huge favor this time.

693
00:32:22,630 --> 00:32:24,430
I've been too ashamed

694
00:32:24,680 --> 00:32:26,400
to come apologize for what happened

695
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:27,790
at the wedding last time.

696
00:32:27,790 --> 00:32:28,850
Alright, alright.

697
00:32:29,270 --> 00:32:31,240
Qin Zhigao, oh, Qin Zhigao.

698
00:32:31,640 --> 00:32:33,570
You have the nerve to bring that up?

699
00:32:34,240 --> 00:32:34,960
Do you know

700
00:32:35,200 --> 00:32:36,640
how many reports I had to write

701
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:38,550
to my superiors just because of this?

702
00:32:38,550 --> 00:32:39,640
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

703
00:32:39,640 --> 00:32:40,590
It'll never happen again.

704
00:32:40,590 --> 00:32:41,320
Never again.

705
00:32:41,640 --> 00:32:43,310
If she dares to make a scene again,
I'll kill her.

706
00:32:43,310 --> 00:32:44,200
No, no, no.

707
00:32:44,550 --> 00:32:45,350
You kill her

708
00:32:46,130 --> 00:32:47,220
and then what?

709
00:32:47,710 --> 00:32:50,440
That's just more trouble for the court,
isn't it?

710
00:32:57,590 --> 00:32:58,750
Didn't I tell you?

711
00:32:58,940 --> 00:32:59,880
I'm not going.

712
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:01,290
I'm not interested.

713
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:04,570
The small court behind the school.

714
00:33:04,920 --> 00:33:05,650
At 6:30.

715
00:33:05,950 --> 00:33:06,810
You can make it.

716
00:33:07,210 --> 00:33:08,810
You want me to pay him a visit?

717
00:33:09,310 --> 00:33:10,700
Are you kidding me?

718
00:33:11,210 --> 00:33:13,210
I'm not asking you to pay him a visit.

719
00:33:14,070 --> 00:33:15,480
He takes a walk every day

720
00:33:15,480 --> 00:33:17,080
and happens to pass by there.

721
00:33:17,480 --> 00:33:19,480
Anyway, I've passed on the message.

722
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:21,460
You're going to Binjiang.

723
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:22,770
Did he really agree?

724
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:23,600
He agreed.

725
00:33:24,400 --> 00:33:26,510
And Mr. Cheng and his wife

726
00:33:26,830 --> 00:33:28,030
are both supportive.

727
00:33:28,350 --> 00:33:28,960
So?

728
00:33:31,650 --> 00:33:32,470
Why should I care

729
00:33:32,470 --> 00:33:33,590
about their opinions?

730
00:33:33,590 --> 00:33:34,190
Honestly.

731
00:33:34,240 --> 00:33:35,240
You don't care,

732
00:33:35,350 --> 00:33:36,880
but you just asked about it.

733
00:33:37,400 --> 00:33:37,830
Right?

734
00:33:38,030 --> 00:33:38,590
Yizhong.

735
00:33:40,110 --> 00:33:40,750
Mrs. Song

736
00:33:40,750 --> 00:33:41,930
gave us a bag of rice.

737
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:43,110
Come with me to get it.

738
00:33:43,110 --> 00:33:43,550
Okay.

739
00:33:45,750 --> 00:33:46,310
Dad.

740
00:33:49,270 --> 00:33:51,310
The times are pushing us forward.

741
00:33:51,350 --> 00:33:52,830
Don't carry the past with you forever.

742
00:33:52,830 --> 00:33:53,550
Just go.

743
00:33:54,440 --> 00:33:55,510
Grudges and all that,

744
00:33:55,510 --> 00:33:56,770
you should let them go.

745
00:34:17,360 --> 00:34:17,960
Mom.

746
00:34:18,860 --> 00:34:19,920
Why is my dad always

747
00:34:19,920 --> 00:34:21,520
butting heads with Mr. Zhou?

748
00:34:23,510 --> 00:34:25,440
Your dad doesn't want to talk about it.

749
00:34:25,440 --> 00:34:26,440
As for Zhou,

750
00:34:26,600 --> 00:34:27,330
he also feels

751
00:34:27,360 --> 00:34:28,960
it's a matter for their generation.

752
00:34:28,960 --> 00:34:30,670
He doesn't want to
bring it up with you either.

753
00:34:30,670 --> 00:34:31,929
Then whose fault is it?

754
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:33,480
Definitely your dad's.

755
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:35,330
Zhou did nothing wrong.

756
00:34:36,150 --> 00:34:37,080
Tell me about it.

757
00:35:34,330 --> 00:35:35,040
Zhou

758
00:35:35,070 --> 00:35:36,840
is only a few years older than your dad.

759
00:35:36,840 --> 00:35:37,630
But

760
00:35:37,930 --> 00:35:39,440
he was your dad's counselor

761
00:35:39,440 --> 00:35:40,370
back in college.

762
00:35:40,850 --> 00:35:41,560
And

763
00:35:41,590 --> 00:35:43,250
they were very close friends.

764
00:35:46,410 --> 00:35:47,280
These two

765
00:35:47,880 --> 00:35:49,140
are about the same age.

766
00:35:49,230 --> 00:35:50,880
Both loved playing basketball,

767
00:35:50,880 --> 00:35:53,080
and shared pretty similar views on law.

768
00:35:53,440 --> 00:35:55,970
But their backgrounds were
quite different.

769
00:35:57,110 --> 00:35:58,550
Zhou came from

770
00:35:58,960 --> 00:36:00,890
a politically impeccable family—

771
00:36:01,110 --> 00:36:02,710
born to a poor peasant household.

772
00:36:02,710 --> 00:36:03,670
But your dad

773
00:36:04,030 --> 00:36:05,070
was from a landlord family.

774
00:36:05,070 --> 00:36:05,920
Back then,

775
00:36:06,150 --> 00:36:07,950
that was a real mark against you.

776
00:36:09,630 --> 00:36:10,560
Hello, Chen Fan.

777
00:36:14,590 --> 00:36:15,710
Back in 1957,

778
00:36:16,190 --> 00:36:18,120
everyone was watching their back.

779
00:36:18,710 --> 00:36:20,110
Your dad could've easily

780
00:36:20,190 --> 00:36:22,050
been labeled a rightist himself.

781
00:36:22,070 --> 00:36:23,400
Afraid of dragging me down,

782
00:36:23,400 --> 00:36:25,260
he brought up breaking up with me.

783
00:36:26,110 --> 00:36:27,970
There was no way I was having that.

784
00:36:28,150 --> 00:36:29,060
No matter what,

785
00:36:29,250 --> 00:36:29,970
your mom

786
00:36:30,190 --> 00:36:31,000
was young once

787
00:36:31,590 --> 00:36:33,190
and burned for love.

788
00:36:34,150 --> 00:36:35,550
But right at that moment,

789
00:36:35,760 --> 00:36:38,560
someone in the department was out
to get Zhou Yipu.

790
00:36:38,670 --> 00:36:40,320
Your dad, in a moment of weakness,

791
00:36:40,320 --> 00:36:41,150
handed over

792
00:36:41,150 --> 00:36:42,280
the article

793
00:36:42,690 --> 00:36:43,750
Zhou had given him.

794
00:36:45,030 --> 00:36:45,810
In the end,

795
00:36:45,840 --> 00:36:47,230
some words in the article

796
00:36:47,230 --> 00:36:48,890
were twisted into charges against him.

797
00:36:48,890 --> 00:36:50,670
So Mr. Zhou was branded a rightist

798
00:36:50,670 --> 00:36:51,670
because of my dad?

799
00:36:54,150 --> 00:36:56,480
That's what your dad has always believed.

800
00:36:57,100 --> 00:36:58,140
But I think

801
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:00,400
even if your dad hadn't said

802
00:37:00,400 --> 00:37:01,400
or done anything,

803
00:37:01,840 --> 00:37:03,670
things wouldn't have
turned out differently.

804
00:37:03,670 --> 00:37:05,960
He'd only been a presiding judge
for a few years

805
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:07,440
before he was singled out and criticized.

806
00:37:07,440 --> 00:37:08,480
We had to take you

807
00:37:08,840 --> 00:37:11,280
and get sent down to a factory
in the third-tier.

808
00:37:11,280 --> 00:37:11,800
Mom,

809
00:37:12,600 --> 00:37:13,370
I don't think

810
00:37:13,400 --> 00:37:15,000
you can just blame the times.

811
00:37:15,030 --> 00:37:16,630
My dad had a choice back then.

812
00:37:17,280 --> 00:37:18,880
Even if it was a difficult choice,

813
00:37:18,880 --> 00:37:20,410
he still could have chosen.

814
00:37:20,880 --> 00:37:21,360
Right?

815
00:37:22,150 --> 00:37:22,960
So,

816
00:37:23,730 --> 00:37:25,550
your dad spent the rest of his life

817
00:37:25,550 --> 00:37:27,680
feeling frustrated and unfulfilled.

818
00:37:28,150 --> 00:37:28,920
But you

819
00:37:29,510 --> 00:37:30,970
are his one and only pride.

820
00:37:31,930 --> 00:37:33,320
You encouraged my son to return

821
00:37:33,320 --> 00:37:35,450
to Binjiang to be a lawyer, didn't you?

822
00:37:38,480 --> 00:37:39,590
He is an adult.

823
00:37:40,480 --> 00:37:42,030
He has the right to choose

824
00:37:42,030 --> 00:37:43,160
his own path in life.

825
00:37:43,760 --> 00:37:44,830
Right or wrong,

826
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:47,510
that's for him to decide.

827
00:37:48,960 --> 00:37:49,890
Don't you think?

828
00:37:50,850 --> 00:37:51,850
He is my son.

829
00:37:51,880 --> 00:37:52,980
He is my student.

830
00:37:53,070 --> 00:37:54,800
So you think I should

831
00:37:55,510 --> 00:37:57,310
understand my dad's cowardice?

832
00:37:57,320 --> 00:37:57,920
No.

833
00:37:58,880 --> 00:38:01,150
It's precisely because
you're an upright person

834
00:38:01,150 --> 00:38:02,750
that your dad is proud of you.

835
00:38:04,160 --> 00:38:05,490
And I'm proud of you too.

836
00:38:06,360 --> 00:38:08,000
Because you made many choices

837
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:10,400
that your dad never had
the courage to make.

838
00:38:22,070 --> 00:38:23,730
You even brought backup, huh?

839
00:38:34,440 --> 00:38:35,640
Remember this place?

840
00:38:37,030 --> 00:38:37,980
Of course I do.

841
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:40,400
This is where you all gathered

842
00:38:40,400 --> 00:38:41,730
before being sent down.

843
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:43,850
This is where I got on the bus

844
00:38:44,150 --> 00:38:45,550
to go to the cadre school.

845
00:38:46,320 --> 00:38:47,480
This should have always been

846
00:38:47,480 --> 00:38:49,010
a place to play basketball.

847
00:38:50,320 --> 00:38:51,710
Although it's now old

848
00:38:52,960 --> 00:38:53,760
and run-down,

849
00:38:54,920 --> 00:38:55,880
but still...

850
00:39:07,110 --> 00:39:07,910
One more game?

851
00:39:09,800 --> 00:39:10,760
No more talking?

852
00:39:13,630 --> 00:39:14,490
Same old rules.

853
00:39:14,710 --> 00:39:15,910
You take the tip‑off.

854
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:20,500
Don't go easy on me.

855
00:39:25,630 --> 00:39:26,320
I win.

856
00:39:26,320 --> 00:39:26,920
Okay.

857
00:39:28,400 --> 00:39:29,530
You, you... This...

858
00:39:32,550 --> 00:39:33,070
Chen.

859
00:39:34,320 --> 00:39:35,480
How is your blood pressure?

860
00:39:35,480 --> 00:39:36,940
My blood pressure is fine.

861
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:37,840
But my heart

862
00:39:38,630 --> 00:39:39,590
keeps acting up.

863
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:40,930
My heart is okay.

864
00:39:41,630 --> 00:39:43,560
But I just had lumbar spine surgery

865
00:39:43,760 --> 00:39:44,820
a couple years ago.

866
00:39:45,840 --> 00:39:46,630
But it's okay.

867
00:39:46,630 --> 00:39:47,590
Come on, keep going.

868
00:39:47,590 --> 00:39:48,070
Come on.

